cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: >-
  ml-guide-hdac: code for "Machine learning-guided design and synthesis of benzimidazole-based
  HDAC inhibitors: prospective validation of a fine-tuned pretrained graph transformer"
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying the manuscript. A pretrained GROVER graph transformer is fine-tuned on HDAC
  activity data and used, as a three-classifier ensemble, to prioritise synthetically accessible
  candidates from sixty designed compounds; series IX was the only series predicted active by all
  three classifiers, and all six members were synthesised and biologically evaluated. The
  repository loads the distributed models and reproduces the held-out benchmark, the five-fold
  cross-validation and the virtual screening, checking every output against committed reference
  values.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ai-drugs-hup/ml-guide-hdac"
keywords:
  - HDAC
  - histone deacetylase
  - GROVER
  - graph transformer
  - molecular representation
  - transfer learning
  - virtual screening
  - QSAR
  - benzimidazole
  - hydroxamic acid
  - cheminformatics
